{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Managing the Restaurant"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Looking at Resumes"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 5}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Express duty, advice, willingness, or intention to do something in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le05ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "When + Present Perfect and If"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">when</span> and <span class=\"italic\">if</span> to talk about conditions that will be fulfilled before a situation can happen. <br/><br/>You use <span class=\"italic\">when</span> with the Present Perfect to talk about a condition that needs to be completed before another one can occur."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can also use <span class=\"italic\">when</span> with the Present Perfect to suggest that something needs to happen before something else can happen. In that context, <span class=\"italic\">when</span> has the meaning of <span class=\"italic\">as soon as</span>, <span class=\"italic\">after</span>, <span class=\"italic\">until</span>. <br/> <span class=\"strong\">Example</span>: <span class=\"italic\">We'll get started <span class=\"strong\">when </span>everyone <span class=\"strong\">has arrived</span>.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You normally use <span class=\"italic\">if</span> with the Present Simple in an if clause to talk about a possible outcome. The outcome will be positive if the condition in the if clause is fulfilled.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Example</span>: <span class=\"italic\">We'll get better reviews <span class=\"strong\">if</span> everyone <span class=\"strong\">works</span> a little harder.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the examples from the text:"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Keep your interactions pleasant even when a customer has been unreasonable and rude. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you are a waitress, a bartender or a cook, you have to be able to prepare and deliver food to specifications."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you are easily flustered, you will become overwhelmed. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You will be called on to cover the Sunday shift if we are short on staff."}, {"type": "example", "content": "When you have finished taking their order, you need to get table two more drinks."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You'll need to help up front, when they've left."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Modals for Duty or Obligation in the Past"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use a variety of modals to talk about duties and obligations, to express what someone is responsible for and to give strong advice and recommendations. <br/> <br/>You use <span class=\"italic\">should</span> and <span class=\"italic\">have to</span> to express duty and obligation in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Let's look at the modals<span class=\"italic\"> must</span>, <span class=\"italic\">have to</span>, <span class=\"italic\">have got to</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">should</span>. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You cannot use <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">must</span></span> to express duty or obligation in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">should</span> + have + past participle to express duty in the past.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Example</span>: <span class=\"italic\">You should have told me about your problems with the customers yesterday</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">had to</span> and before verbs that talk about necessity. <span class=\"italic\">Had to</span> implies that someone else imposed the necessity on you.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Example</span>: <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">had to</span> leave the kitchen completely clean before you left</span>. = It implies that it was a duty to leave the kitchen clean, and it may not have been fulfilled."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read the following examples from the text:"}, {"type": "example", "content": "My former restaurant employees should have been able to handle multiple orders from multiple tables simultaneously, but they couldn't."}, {"type": "example", "content": "They should have memorized the specials."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You should have handled that in a delicate, friendly manner. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We had to provide that service in a friendly manner. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I had to put in another round of drinks while fetching more napkins."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "high-pressure "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "needing to work very hard"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: Restaurant employees are faced with a high-pressure customer service position. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob09aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when talking about restaurant staff."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "busboy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a young man whose job is to take away dirty dishes from the tables in a restaurant"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The primary goal of any restaurant employee, from manager to busboy, is to provide excellent service to their customers."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob09aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "specification"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a detailed instruction about how something should be made "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You have to be able to prepare and deliver food to specifications."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob09aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to diminish"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to become or make something become smaller or less; to reduce"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:You run the risk of diminishing your restaurant's reputation."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob09aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "proliferation "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "sudden increase in the amount or number of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Keep in mind the proliferation of food allergies among patron."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob09aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "round of "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "drinks for a \u200bgroup of \u200bpeople  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  You may have to put in another round of drinks."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob09aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "set"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "fixed"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: While you may have a set schedule, that schedule is almost always subject to change."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob09aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to call on"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to ask someone to do something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You can work Friday and Saturday only to be called on to cover the Sunday shift."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le05ob09aud08"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online for information on how to write a resume."}, {"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, answer the following questions: What is a resume?, What information should be included?, How long should it be?, What are references?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at sample resumes online as well."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Create your own resume using your personal experiences."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your resume with a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I discuss the features of a resume."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read samples of resumes."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I create my own resume."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my resume with a partner."}]}], "labs": [{"type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0}, {"type": "audio", "title": "", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn11le05ob09re2img01.jpg ", "text": "", "id": 0}, {"time": "1", "image": "engenn11le05ob09re2img01.jpg ", "text": "Not everyone can handle working in a restaurant. Restaurant employees are faced with a high-pressure customer service position that should be handled in a delicate, friendly\nmanner. To be a successful restaurant employee, you must possess certain traits.", "id": 1}, {"time": "13500", "image": "engenn11le05ob09re2img02.jpg ", "text": "The primary goal of any restaurant employee, from manager to busboy, is to provide excellent service to their customers. People go to restaurants for a night off from cooking and perhaps, cleaning, making the experience almost as important as the food. As a restaurant employee, it is your job to provide that service in a friendly manner. Keep your interactions pleasant even when a customer has been unreasonable or rude. Remember that you represent the restaurant and not just yourself.", "id": 2}, {"time": "45000", "image": "engenn11le05ob09re2img02.jpg ", "text": "Not everyone likes their steak cooked the same way. Nor does everyone want a lemon in their soda. If you are a waitress, a bartender or a cook, you have to be able to prepare and deliver food to specifications. Otherwise, you run the risk of diminishing your restaurant's reputation. Some restaurants even require wait staff to memorize specials and take orders without writing them down. Keeping in mind the proliferation of food allergies among patrons, something as innocuous as leaving peanuts on a sundae can be a potential health risk opening your eatery up  to liability.", "id": 3}, {"time": "82000", "image": "engenn11le05ob09re2img03.jpg ", "text": "Accuracy is a challenge in and of itself. This is exacerbated when you consider a restaurant employee must be able to handle multiple orders from multiple tables simultaneously. You may have to put in another round of drinks while fetching more napkins and checking on why table seven's food isn't ready yet. You must be able  to handle these tasks with efficiency and poise. If you are easily flustered, you will become overwhelmed.", "id": 4}, {"time": "109000", "image": "engenn11le05ob09re2img03.jpg ", "text": "Restaurant employees rarely work 9 to 5. While you may have a set schedule, that schedule is almost always subject to change. As a high turnover industry, personnel is  always changing.  You can work Friday and Saturday only to be called on to cover the Sunday shift or you maybe be scheduled to work until closing at midnight only to find yourself working until the last table leaves at quarter to one.", "id": 5}], "audiosrc": "engenn11le05ob09re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn11le05ob09re2img01.jpg "}}], "id": 2}], "exercises": [{"type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Do you like interacting with people? Why or why not? "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Would you work in a restaurant? What would you do?"}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about work and dealing with customers."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can express that a fairly certain condition will be fulfilled using when or if. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can express duty or obligation in the past. "}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct"}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Do you have what it takes to work in the restaurant industry? "}], "stimuli_ids": [0], "questions": [], "id": 0}, {"type": "STI", "stimuli_ids": [2], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "responses": [{"correct": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [